"""Analyze MySQL/MariaDB binary logs and report operation counts per table.

How it works
------------
1. Select the binary logs that can contain events in the requested time window.
2. Run ``mysqlbinlog`` once per log file (in parallel) and *stream* its output,
   counting INSERT / UPDATE / DELETE / TRUNCATE / DROP operations per table in
   a single pass. Nothing decoded is ever written to disk.
3. Merge the per-file counters and write a report plus a list of analyzed logs.
4. Optionally (--write-queries) also collect sample SQL queries per operation and
   table and write them to one file per operation type.

Optional GUI
------------
Started with ``--gui`` the tool opens a small tkinter window instead of
running on the command line. ``tkinter`` is imported only in that case, so the normal
command line mode does not depend on it. Any other options given together with
``--gui`` are used as the initial values of the form.
"""

